Z||000000||PeaceDawg||05-30-2001||07:06 PM||||Anyone know of any existing Fiero Clubs in and around Ottawa Canada?  I know of 2.  One guy I contacted says he is too busy to be running his and there isn't much left (to his club I guess) and I haven't recieved any email back from the other club.  Are there any clubs in Ottawa that actually meet?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Jay||05-30-2001||07:07 PM||||Don't know of any in Ottawa, but would you be willing to come to Toronto?  <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/gtaclub/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.home.net/gtaclub/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gangster.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||05-30-2001||07:22 PM||||Gosh --- There should be!  I see lots of them whenever I am in town!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||05-30-2001||07:31 PM||||Nicolas Matjasko lives in Pakenham , has a bunch of Fiero's including some wild 396 cu in v8 small block Fiero with a 4spd auto. He may be able to help you , there used to be a club , but I don't think it ever got off the ground. There is also another fellow with a very stock sedate looking 86 GT with a 3.4, his name escapes me..<BR>This is nicks email , his godfather is also into fiero's<BR>Ther else also a guy named Lui who lives in the ottawa area who sells parts and has a wharehouse full of stuff. I bought a set of GT rims from him.<P>This is nicks email , his godfather is also into fiero's<P>matjasko@sympatico.ca<P>I also just had someone join the Fiero racing list who is in the ottawa area , I will try to find out more aboutwhen i get a chance to email this person<P>Hope this helps<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RaidenCobra||05-30-2001||10:31 PM||||On the topic:<BR>Is there any clubs in London?<BR>I mean I Would join Toronto's club but thats a hell of a hike for me.. <BR>Although I could stop by Area 51 Paintball and get a few games in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000005||PeaceDawg||05-31-2001||07:01 PM||||Jay...Toronto I think is a little too far.<BR>Slammed Fiero...I know Lui, he lives just up the road from me and he certainly has some nice cars.  That is interesting about your friend in Packenham.  I am gonna take down the email and give him a shout.  Thanks everyone.  I am gonna keep investigating...There has to be an existing club in the Ottawa area somewhere.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Urchin||05-31-2001||09:14 PM||||RaidenCobra:  There are a bunch of us from London and surrounding area cruising to Grand Bend, which I think I saw your responce on the post, but anyways, something formal may come of it, who knows.  By the way, if you don't know about it, it's at Best's Ise Cream in Grand Bend, June 9th at 1:00.  Some of us are meeting at 11:00 at Spring Bank Park before hand.  So come on out.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_8.jpg"> ||||reg||1
